{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>These you shall offer to YHWH at your appointed seasons, besides your vows and your freewill offerings.</b> It would have been fitting for Scripture to say 'for your burnt offerings and for your peace offerings,' which are the flesh offerings, and afterward 'and for your meal offerings and for your libations'; but it placed the עולה first, for it is the offering that always comes first, as the Sages, of blessed memory, expounded: 'the עולה — it comes first,' meaning there is nothing offered before the morning tamid. And it concludes with שלמים, for the שלמים come to perfect the attributes, and it is the way of Scripture to conclude with שלמים, as it is written (Leviticus 7:37): ״זאת התורה לעולה למנחה ולחטאת ולאשם ולמלואים ולזבח השלמים״, and great is the attribute of peace, and it is fitting to conclude with it. And just as it mentioned above the unique Name at the head of the section, so it now mentions it at the end of the section, as it is said: ״אלה תעשו לה'״ and so forth. And it mentioned seventy bulls in the middle to indicate that the intention in all of them is for the unique Name alone; but on the eighth day, which is unique, we offer in it a unique offering, which is a single bull, to the Elohim of Israel, who is a unique Master over a unique people. And this is their saying: 'The seventy bulls — why? Corresponding to the seventy nations,' that is, corresponding to the princes of the seventy nations; 'a single bull — why? Corresponding to a unique nation,' that is, corresponding to the Elohim of a unique nation. Through these offerings the world was blessed, and every force recognizes the force above it, and so from force to force until the supreme Cause, blessed be He, as it is said (Ecclesiastes 5:7): ״כי גבוה מעל גבוה שומר וגבוהים עליהם״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {0 "The second explanation of 'כנגד אומה יחידה' reads 'כגנד אלהי אומה יחידה' in the source; the word כגנד appears to be a typographical error for כנגד, rendered here as 'corresponding to.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:36:54.035533187Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}